Wow.  When people talk about Demogorgon being a nasty fella to fight,
they ain't kidding!

Playing my Dwarven Valkyrie named Xavier (because she was so ugly her
parents thought she was a man) with 171 HP and AC of -49, very little
has been able to pose a significant threat.  Yeenoghu was in the
Valley of the Dean, and was only a hassle because a bunch of Fire
Vampires and a Shoggoth had corroded and burned the hell out of my
armor, but some wishing and magic marker use fixed (in more ways than
one) things right up for me.  With that done, I headed back down,
entering Gehennom Proper for the first time.

The first level was a water maze.  Nothing remarkable there.  My ring
of levitation made mapping it easy as something that's very easy. 
Jubilex was on G3, but I actually ended up almost windshielding him -
he didn't score a single hit on me, and by the time I realized I was
fighting a demon prince, he was reduced to a pile of yuck and slime. 
Mapping the swamp was again easy because of my ring of levitation.

Below that, in G4, was a conventional maze.  Easy enough.  Just follow
the wall, and OH MY GOD, THIS IS DEMOGORGON'S LEVEL!  Luckily my tame
Deva was between me and the big D, so I was able to take off my trusty
ring of levitation, engrave Elbereth with my trusty Athame, and then
give Demogorgon a couple swats with Mojo and Excalibur.  Predictably,
Demogorgon wasn't interested in a fight on those terms, and
immediately teleported to the up stairs.  A quick dash after him and
an exchange of blows left him retreating back up to G3 and me both
stunned and deathly ill and down below 120 HP.  Luckily, I had a
blessed +3 Unicorn Horn handy, and my first attempt to cure the
disease proved successful.

Putting my ring of levitation back on, I zapped myself a few times
with a wand of healing, then gave chase.  What followed was a running
battle across Jubilex's swamp between Demogorgon and I.  Demogorgon
got most of the offense, because I generally would heal as soon as I
got sick, or occasionally after 1 turn of attack if I hadn't gotten
any offense in in a bit.  The general lack of solid ground under my
feet prevented me from using Elbereth to my advantage, so I could only
battle on Demogorgon's terms...

Well, that or run away.  And I wasn't about to run away.  A pitched
battle at the upstairs actually got pretty scary.  Not only did
Demogorgon make me sick, but he hit again and made me feel much worse.
 Twice.  Not a good thing.  Apply Unicorn Horn!  Nothing happens. 
CRAP.  Apply Unicorn Horn!  You feel more steady.  CRAP!  Apply
Unicorn Horn!  What a relief!

NO KIDDING!  I NEARLY HAD A HEART ATTACK THERE!

Another smack with Mojo and Excalibur, and, of course, Demogorgon
retreated up the stairs.

HOW MANY HP DOES THIS GUY HAVE?  I'm doing in the neighborhood of 75
total damage each time I attack!

Once again, I heal up and float upward once again.  G2.  The water
maze.  More running combat with Demogorgon.  And I'm down to 92 HP
without hitting him once.  And I'm ill.  Apply Unicorn Horn!  What a
relief!

Then, suddenly, an opening!  Demogorgon casts a spell to curse
something in my inventory and doesn't manage to make me ill! 
SmacKRACKABOOM!  Slice!  And... HE'S STILL ALIVE!?!  And I'm ill
again.  This is getting old.  Instead of healing, I risk another
attack to try to get him before he ducks up the stairs into the Valley
of the Dead... and... YES!  The invisible Demogorgon is killed!  Apply
Unicorn Horn!  What a relief!

Thank god!  Now THAT... was an intense fight.  I thought I was going
to buy the farm for sure.

Considering I just beat Demogorgon in melee, does that mean I've got a
good shot at ascending if I don't suffer an unfortunate newt-related
mishap?  I've still got quite a bit of Gehennom to go and need to pay
Vlad and Rodney a visit.  Keeping in mind that I'm playing SlashEM, do
I have much to worry about at this point?  (As a side note, I've heard
enough horror stories about nasties casting spells that create pools
of water under you to plan on making use of my Ring of Levitation when
fighting magic using enemies...  Maybe I should bless the ring...)

